From 8884fcc05622df73812f9fb73cd51be9d9d67cf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 20:47:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(emitter): lower parameter defaults when the decorator
 pass hoists in the parameters

tsc-port: visitParameterList @6.0.3 (_tsc.js:91168-91181): the parameters
of a function-like are visited under LexicalEnvironmentFlags.InParameters;
when a temporary is hoisted meanwhile (VariablesHoistedInParameters) and
the target is ES2015 or later, addDefaultValueAssignmentsIfNeeded
(91182-91276) lowers each default: an initializer becomes
`if (name === void 0) { name = initializer; }` (condition name a
positionless clone, assignment target a NoSourceMap clone, the
initializer NoSourceMap | NoComments, assignment and block ranged to the
parameter, block SingleLine | NoTrailingSourceMap | NoTokenSourceMaps |
NoComments) added by addInitializationStatement as a custom prologue, and
a binding pattern is aliased by getGeneratedNameForNode(parameter) with a
`var <pattern> = alias === void 0 ? initializer : alias;` statement; the
parameter loses its initializer. mergeLexicalEnvironment then places the
custom prologues after the hoisted `var` statements.

The Rust decorator pass visited the parameters through the generic child
visit with no window and no lowering, so a named-evaluation hoist from a
parameter initializer left the default in place for class-fields to lower
with its own map ownership (ES2015/ES2022) or not at all (ESNext/set).
`visit_function_like_body` now visits the parameters first under the
window, lowers when hoisted, memoizes the lowered array for the generic
visit, and `merge_block_environment` splices the initialization statements
at leftHoistedVariablesEnd. The binding-pattern branch is the same callee's
unwitnessed arm, implemented without a claim.

Focused run (lexical-prologue-readers-v2, 16 commands, binary built with
causes 5 and 6): 16 exact twice, exit 0, sources and witness inputs
unchanged after the run
(ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-literal-prologue-cause6-focused.v1.json).
